{{!-- Relationships section shell: a Table/Board toggle over ONE of two renderings of the
      same rows. Shared by the NPC sheet's Relationships tab, the character sheet's Details
      tab and the steading sheet's Relationships card.

      Each view gets the params it actually reads: the table takes rows + nameLabel + the
      resizeKey its columns are stored under, the board takes lanes (built over those same
      rows), and both take canRate / canToggle / showTooltip. `view` is the stored layout
      ("table" | "board"); it and `resizeKey` come from the host's getData via
      relationshipViewContext(). `data-rel-view` on the wrapper is what tells
      wireRelationshipBoard whether there are any cards down there to wire.

      The host still decides whether to render this at all — with no rows there is nothing
      for either layout to show, so the empty state stays outside and the toggle goes with it.

      Only ONE view renders. Rendering both and hiding one with CSS would duplicate every
      `data-rel-id` node, including the live note input, so editing the visible copy would
      leave its hidden twin stale and the delegated change handler could not tell them
      apart. The toggle re-renders instead.

      The toolbar renders here ONLY when the host has nowhere better to put it — the NPC
      relationships tab has no heading row at all. The character and steading sheets place
      `stonetop.relationships-viewbar` in their own heading row instead and pass
      `hideViewbar=true`, so the toggle sits on the heading's line rather than below it. Its
      click handler is delegated from the sheet root and finds its table from the button's
      own `data-resize-key`, which is what lets the toolbar move without the wiring moving. --}}
<div class="stonetop-rel-views" data-resize-key="{{this.resizeKey}}" data-rel-view="{{this.view}}">
	{{#unless hideViewbar}}
	{{> "stonetop.relationships-viewbar" resizeKey=resizeKey view=view}}
	{{/unless}}

	{{#if (eq view "board")}}
	{{> "stonetop.relationships-board" lanes=lanes
	    canRate=canRate canToggle=canToggle showTooltip=showTooltip}}
	{{else}}
	{{> "stonetop.relationships-table" rows=rows resizeKey=resizeKey nameLabel=nameLabel
	    canRate=canRate canToggle=canToggle showTooltip=showTooltip}}
	{{/if}}
</div>
